,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"blind_id\":\"ST026\",\"coverage\":[{\"point\":1,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"States that a Rule 485(a)(2) amendment adding a series normally becomes effective 75 calendar days after filing, versus 60 days for other 485(a) amendments, and notes acceleration or a later date can change this. Calls it a 'registration-effectiveness timetable, not an end-to-end launch guarantee' and says the 75-day rule does not apply to a new trust's initial registration.\"},{\"point\":2,\"credit\":0,\"reason\":\"Optional point. No filed example and no explicit statement that shares cannot be sold before effectiveness. This omission does not reduce the grade.\"},{\"point\":3,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"Lists SEC comments and revisions, exchange listing approval, operational readiness, seed capital and service-provider/AP arrangements as factors affecting launch timing. The optional 95-day designated-date limit is omitted, which does not reduce the grade.\"}],\"central_error\":null,\"local_error\":null,\"grade\":\"correct\",\"rationale\":\"Both required points are fully covered. The answer does not apply the 75-day clock to initial trust registration or present it as a launch guarantee. The description of initial registration (SEC review, declaration of effectiveness, delaying amendments) is accurate. Only optional elements are missing.\"}","ttft_ms":3795,"type":"result","duration_ms":7386,"uuid":"41c44f5a-a4f7-4c7a-a700-263b3446451f","ttft_stream_ms":1921,"time_to_request_ms":71,"first_content_frame_ms":1922,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
